<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 2.7 · The Elf Finale" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="2-7" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 2.7</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">The Elf Finale</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Follow the elf story from Regicide to Song of the Elves, carry the useful quest items forward, and enter Prifddinas without inventing a Magic-80 gate. This closes Chapter 2.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Complete Regicide → Roving Elves → Mourning's End Part I → Mourning's End Part II → Song of the Elves, then record the guaranteed Chapter 2 handoff."
        stats={["All eight Song of the Elves skills actual, unboosted 70+ at entry", "Actual 60+ Ranged; 70 Prayer and Defence; 67 Sailing", "No mandatory Magic 80, Blood Blitz, brew supply or catalytic-talisman drop"]}
        unlocks={["Crystal equipment choice and Lletya access", "Death Altar and Temple of Light completion", "Prifddinas, crystal-city travel and activities"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Start from the real 2.6 exit, not a projected level.</strong> Check the skill tab for actual, unboosted <strong>70+ Agility, Construction, Farming, Herblore, Hunter, Mining, Smithing and Woodcutting</strong>. Also confirm <strong>60+ Ranged, 70 Prayer, 70 Defence, Piety, 67 Sailing</strong>, Barrows gloves, dragon defender, Ava's accumulator, upgraded Iban's staff, full Fairytale II, Making History and the completed quest chains from 2.1–2.6. The camphor-hulled skiff and other retained Chapter 2 kit stay banked where appropriate. If a real gate is missing, finish its earlier route checkpoint before proceeding; this page adds no new skill grind.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Tirannwn · the first crossing</div><h2>Prepare for a long trip and make tomorrow's naphtha today.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i27-regicide" number="1" title="Complete Regicide; bank a second barrel of naphtha">
        <p>Start with King Lathas in Ardougne Castle after <strong>Underground Pass</strong>; actual 70 Agility exceeds Regicide's 56 traversal gate. For the first Underground Pass/Tirannwn trip take a <strong>bow and arrows, two ropes (three is a comfortable buffer), spade, tinderbox, food, antipoison, teleports and combat gear</strong>. Take an axe if you want to cook the rabbit available on the route. The forests have poison traps, hostile creatures and no convenient first-trip bank. Fight the level-110 Tyras guard from a safe distance with Ranged or Magic if your melee gear is modest. The <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Regicide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Regicide route map</a> is worth keeping open for the forest and Underground Pass crossings.</p>
        <p>At the Iorwerth camp collect <strong>at least three empty barrels</strong> as loss/variance buffer, fill at least two with <strong>coal tar</strong> in the Poison Waste, and collect sulphur. After returning east, get <strong>limestone (not a limestone brick)</strong>, a <strong>pot, gloves, pestle and mortar</strong>, and a <strong>strip of cloth made from four balls of wool at a loom</strong>—a bolt of cloth is not the fuse. Keep the Big Book O' Bangs for the Chemist in Rimmington. At his fractionalising still, distil <strong>two separate barrels of coal tar</strong>: each uses roughly <strong>5–9 coal</strong>, so bring about 20 coal plus a buffer, hold pressure and heat in the green, and add coal gradually. Turn <em>one</em> naphtha into the barrel bomb with ground sulphur, pot of quicklime and cloth. <strong>Bank the second, unfinished barrel of naphtha for Mourning's End Part I.</strong> Do not add sulphur or quicklime to that one. Finish Regicide with the bomb and bank/regear afterward; the extra naphtha is the intentional carryover, not a reason to hoard every quest item.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i27-roving" number="2" title="Complete Roving Elves; choose crystal shield by default">
        <p><strong>Regicide and Waterfall Quest</strong> are complete. Use Tirannwn access (or the Port Tyras charter) to find Islwyn and Eluned; carry food, antipoison and travel supplies for Isafdar. Check for <strong>Glarial's pebble</strong> from Waterfall Quest; retrieve it via the Tree Gnome Village dungeon if missing. Also stage a <strong>spade, rope and the Waterfall Dungeon key</strong> from its crates. For Glarial's Tomb, bank <strong>all weapons, armour, runes and ammunition</strong>—even a staff or rune stack blocks entry. Food and potions are allowed. Kill a level-84 Moss Guardian <strong>unarmed and unarmoured</strong> for the consecration seed, then use the Waterfall tomb and return to the elves. Bank/regear between the tomb and Tirannwn portions. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Roving_Elves" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest guide</a>.</p>
        <p>At the reward choice, <strong>crystal shield</strong> is the default immediate-use pick: it needs <strong>70 Defence and 50 Agility</strong>, which this route already has. The <strong>crystal bow</strong> needs <strong>70 Ranged and 50 Agility</strong>; only 60 Ranged is guaranteed here. Bow is fine if your optional play reached 70 Ranged or you simply prefer it. <strong>Neither choice changes the mandatory route.</strong> See the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Crystal_shield" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">shield</a> and <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Crystal_bow" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">bow</a> requirements.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Mourner infiltration</div><h2>One disguise, two quests—do not lose the outfit.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i27-mep1" number="3" title="Complete Mourning's End Part I; retain every mourner piece">
        <p>Before starting, check <strong>Roving Elves, Big Chompy Bird Hunting and Sheep Herder</strong> complete, plus <strong>actual 60 Ranged and actual 50 Thieving</strong>. These are mandatory-route guarantees. Stage the <strong>second barrel of naphtha from Regicide</strong>, two silk, bear fur (obtainable near Jorral's Outpost), one each of red/yellow/green/blue dye (buy at the Lletya Seamstress; extras cover missed shots), bucket of water, feather, magic log, soft leather, toad crunchies or premade t'd crunch, and travel/food. Get the quest-specific rotten apple north-west of the Mourner HQ and ogre bellows during the quest. Leave <strong>seven inventory spaces</strong> to receive the outfit. If the bank has no magic log, collect one from existing Wintertodt loot or a repeatable Hunter-rumour reward before this phase; do not assume a prior reward roll.</p>
        <p>Defeat a mourner near Arandar for the disguise; its potion lowers combat stats and Hitpoints to 20, so restore or regear before danger. Clean the bloody top with Tegid's soap and water; have Oronwen repair the trousers using the silk and bear fur. Wear the full mourner set to enter the West Ardougne HQ. The captive gnome fixes the device with the feather, leather, log and crunchies; dye swamp toads with bellows and use the device on all four sheep groups. Finally, combine the <strong>banked naphtha</strong> with the quest's rotten-apple mix, sieve it and cook the toxic naphtha on a <strong>range, not a fire</strong>; place the resulting powder in two grain sacks. Return to Arianwyn to <strong>finish MEP1 completely</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Mourning%27s_End_Part_I" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest guide</a>.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>KEEP THE FULL MOURNER OUTFIT, including the gas mask.</strong> Mourning's End Part II and Song of the Elves both use the disguise. Bank it intact after this quest; plague clothing is not a substitute.</div>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i27-death-altar" number="4" title="Audit Death Altar access before committing to the Temple of Light">
        <p>First search the bank for a <strong>death talisman/tiara, catalytic talisman/tiara, or another currently valid altar-access item</strong> such as a Runecraft cape. Use one if you already own it. <strong>Guardians of the Rift access is not a guaranteed catalytic-talisman drop.</strong> If the bank has none, Thorgel's <strong>50-item exchange</strong> is the mandatory deterministic Ironman fallback. His list is <strong>47 fixed items plus one randomly selected ticket, one book and one key</strong>. Audit the fixed items before entering; Thorgel tells you which variant of each final three he wants. Bring them in multiple bank trips, not one impossible inventory. See the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Mourning%27s_End_Part_II#The_Death_Altar" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current altar section</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Thorgel's complete 50-item bank audit" label="Mandatory fallback list">
          <p><strong>47 fixed items:</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Babydragon bones, ball of wool, bronze bar, bronze med helm, bucket of milk, cake tin, cheese, chisel.</li>
            <li>Cooked meat, egg, facemask, fishing rod, flax, gold ring, hammer, iron axe, iron nails, iron pickaxe.</li>
            <li>Jug of wine, kebab, knife, leather boots, leather gloves, lobster pot, lockpick, necklace mould, needle, oak logs.</li>
            <li>Pie dish, plank, pot of flour, potato cactus, <strong>potatoes(10) sack</strong>, pure essence, redberries, rope.</li>
            <li>Rotten tomato, shears, skull, spade, swamp paste, thread, tinderbox, unicorn horn dust, vial of water, white apron, white berries.</li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Three assigned variants:</strong> one of <strong>archery ticket / new Agility arena ticket / Castle wars ticket</strong>; one of <strong>crumbling tome / slashed or battered book / Prifddinas' history</strong>; and one of <strong>jail key / dusty key / Witch's House door key</strong>. The books are recoverable from a POH bookcase; obtain only the ticket and key Thorgel actually assigns. An archery ticket comes from the Ranging Guild target range, a <em>new</em> Agility arena ticket from tagging a Brimhaven dispenser, or a Castle Wars ticket from that minigame. The jail key drops from the Taverley Dungeon jailer; the dusty key can be bought at the Legends' Guild or obtained from Velrak; Witch's House door key is under its front-door pot. For awkward fixed supplies, baby blue dragons in Taverley Dungeon provide babydragon bones, the Kalphite Lair has a potato-cactus ground spawn (bring rope and antipoison), and white berries grow around Isafdar. Check the bank before making any of these trips. The current <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Mourning%27s_End_Part_II" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest guide</a> has exact directions.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i27-mep2" number="5" title="Solve the Temple of Light and complete Mourning's End Part II">
        <p>Take <strong>full mourner gear, chisel, rope, food, Prayer restores, teleports and bank access</strong>; energy or stamina support is useful. Actual 70 Agility reduces obstacle trouble, while 70 Prayer plus <strong>Protect from Melee</strong> protects against the Temple's aggressive shadows. Start with Arianwyn in Lletya, enter the HQ in disguise, take Essyllt's <strong>new key</strong>, then reach the Temple through the dark-beast tunnels. Collect the journal and blackened crystal; chisel the crystal and have Arianwyn turn it into the <strong>newly made crystal</strong> needed at the end.</p>
        <p>The light puzzle has <strong>multiple sections</strong>: hand mirrors turn beams between pillars, coloured crystals change beams, and correctly coloured beams open doors to more mirrors, crystals and chests. Keep the mirrors/crystals you have collected and the newly made crystal; <strong>puzzle mirrors and crystals cannot be banked</strong>. Allow several free inventory slots early and up to roughly 13 near the last section. You can leave and regear between sections—the puzzle state persists—but follow the guide's <strong>cyan-door mirror position before teleporting out for Thorgel bank trips</strong>, or you can lock yourself out of the short return path. If using the 50-item route, give Thorgel his requested items over multiple trips, obtain the death talisman, return with the newly made crystal, and complete the altar sequence. If you brought a valid talisman, skip the exchange. Finish the quest and bank the mourner gear for Song. Use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Mourning%27s_End_Part_II" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">mirror-by-mirror guide</a> for placements; this route gives the preparation and safe stopping points, not a second diagram.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Song of the Elves · hard stop</div><h2>Confirm the true gate, then assemble the whole quest kit.</h2></section>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Do not start Song yet if any gate is missing.</strong> Confirm <strong>Mourning's End Part II, Making History and Druidic Ritual</strong> complete, and actual/unboosted <strong>70 Agility, 70 Construction, 70 Farming, 70 Herblore, 70 Hunter, 70 Mining, 70 Smithing and 70 Woodcutting</strong>. None of those eight level checks accepts a temporary boost. Return to the corresponding <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-6/`}>2.6 method</a> if short; do not create a new 2.7 grind. Song has no 80-Magic requirement.</div>
      <RouteStep id="i27-song-kit" number="6" title="Bank-audit every Song of the Elves quest item">
        <p><strong>Ardougne disguise:</strong> steel full helm, steel platebody, steel platelegs, red dye, purple dye and one silk. <strong>Mourner phase:</strong> the <em>full</em> retained mourner set including gas mask (plague jacket/trousers do not work), plus a tinderbox. <strong>Waterfall offerings:</strong> rope, nature rune, flowers grown from mithril/adamant seeds <em>or one irit leaf</em>, an adamant chainbody (consumed), wine of Zamorak <em>or a Zamorak brew(4)</em>, cabbage (can be picked during the quest), and a black knife <em>or black dagger</em>. <strong>Lletya/Prif preparation:</strong> one cadantine seed, seed dibber unless the relevant Barbarian Farming step is complete, runite bar, vial of water, pestle and mortar, hammer, pickaxe, then <strong>eight limestone bricks, saw, axe and spade</strong>. Lay these out by phase; you do not need every item in one inventory. This is the current <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Song_of_the_Elves" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">required-item list</a>, not an assumption that a bank already contains the odd pieces.</p>
        <p><strong>Ironman sourcing:</strong> if no runite bar is banked, buy <strong>unnoted rune platelegs from Scavvo's Rune Store in the Champions' Guild for 64,000 coins</strong>, place them in the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Nest_(nice)" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">nice nest atop Aldarin windmill</a>, log out or hop, then search the nest for <strong>one runite bar</strong>; no 85 Smithing or rare drop is needed. Check bank and Farming Guild seed vault for the <strong>cadantine seed</strong> first; if absent, use repeatable <strong>Master Farmer pickpockets</strong> (38 Thieving gate already cleared) or continue Farming Contracts/seed packs until one appears. Those are RNG sources, so do not promise a fixed number of attempts. Buy the <strong>adamant chainbody at Wayne's Chains in southern Falador</strong> and the <strong>eight limestone bricks from Keldagrim's Stonemason</strong>. Ordinary armour shops cover steel pieces; Lletya's Seamstress or Aggie supplies dyes, and red plus blue makes purple. For the offerings, a banked <strong>irit leaf</strong> is simpler than growing flowers; telegrab a wine of Zamorak from the non-Wilderness Asgarnia Chaos Temple if necessary; buy a <strong>black dagger at Varrock Swordshop</strong> if neither accepted black blade is banked. Check all items before the first story phase.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i27-seren-kit" number="7" title="Prepare Iban, phoenix necklaces and stackable nightshade for Seren">
        <p>The default no-brews setup is <strong>upgraded Iban's staff with Iban Blast</strong> on the standard spellbook (<strong>50 Magic; five fire runes and one death rune per cast</strong>), around <strong>15–20 phoenix necklaces</strong>, <strong>20+ stackable nightshade</strong>, <strong>2–4 Prayer potions</strong>, <strong>1–2 multi-heal food options</strong> such as Guthix rest or strawberry baskets, and <strong>50+ throwing knives or chinchompas</strong> for the 1-HP healing pillars. Bring enough Iban charges and runes for repeated attempts, an emergency teleport, and Magic-accuracy gear (roughly +50 Magic attack if your level/gear is modest). These are preparation ranges from the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Fragment_of_Seren#Phoenix_necklaces" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current low-level strategy</a>, not a required 20-necklace grind if a smaller stock works for you.</p>
        <p><strong>Necklaces:</strong> check banked diamonds and existing phoenix necklaces first. At <strong>56 Crafting</strong>, use a diamond, gold bar and necklace mould on a furnace; at <strong>57 Magic</strong>, Lvl-4 Enchant each diamond necklace with <strong>one cosmic and ten earth runes</strong>. If short on diamonds, mine repeatable <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Shilo_Village_mine" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Shilo Village gem rocks</a> (already unlocked) or spend banked Shooting Star stardust on <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Bag_full_of_gems" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">40-gem bags</a> at 300 stardust each. Diamond yield is random; gather only the measured shortfall.</p>
        <p><strong>Nightshade:</strong> check bank and seed vault for <strong>belladonna seeds</strong> and plant them early at the <strong>Draynor Manor or Auburnvale belladonna patch</strong>; actual 70 Farming clears its 63 gate. Harvest with gloves. One crop gives <strong>6–18 stackable nightshade</strong>, so two good harvests may cover 20, but check the actual yield and replant if short. If no seed is banked, catch <strong>nature implings</strong> (58 Hunter, already cleared; their jars can contain belladonna seed) or repeat <strong>Master Farmer pickpockets / Farming Contracts</strong> until one appears. None is guaranteed from prior play. Free cave nightshade is an emergency fallback, but it is <strong>unstackable</strong> and displaces necklace/restore slots. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Nightshade" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Nightshade reference</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">The rebellion and final fight</div><h2>Bank between story phases; enter Seren with a rehearsed cycle.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i27-song" number="8" title="Complete Song of the Elves; unlock Prifddinas">
        <p>Start with Arianwyn in Lletya, then follow the Ardougne/Edmond and Elena story using the steel knight disguise. Move through the West Ardougne rebellion in mourner gear and the Waterfall Dungeon's six-offering pillar puzzle. Bank between these phases; do not drag all quest items through every fight. In the Lletya/Prif preparation, plant the cadantine seed, use the runite bar and hammer on the elderly elf's exoskeleton, and make the inversion potion with the elder cadantine and crystal dust. The Grand Library and city preparation lead into hostile combat. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Song_of_the_Elves" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Full quest guide</a>.</p>
        <p>For the <strong>Arianwyn</strong> fight, take sensible food/restores and Ranged or Melee gear; move off his orange ground attacks and watch the purple attack that disables Prayer. Regear before the <strong>Underground Pass siege and Essyllt</strong>: multiple enemies make Prayer, food and supply management important. The quest moves toward Seren after the siege; you can <strong>teleport out after the transition/cutscene to bank and build the dedicated Seren inventory</strong> rather than force the boss with leftover siege supplies. The <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Song_of_the_Elves/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">phase guide</a> gives exact dialogue and puzzle clicks.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Unsafe-death storage:</strong> items lost during Song's major instanced fights can be reclaimed from the <strong>Rebel Scout for 80,000 coins</strong> (the fee may come from your bank). For Seren, the Scout appears <strong>outside the boss entrance</strong>. Reclaim items <strong>before dying anywhere else</strong>; another unsafe death while the Scout still holds them can delete that stash. Do not use a new fight as a recovery shortcut. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Item_Retrieval_Service" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current retrieval rule</a>.</div>
        <p><strong>Understand Seren's repeat:</strong> keep <strong>Protect from Missiles</strong> up for normal projectiles (their max drops to 3+3); on her first special she teleports you beside her, so step away before the rapid melee hits. On the second, attack the <strong>lighter-coloured real clone</strong>. On the third, rapidly tag each red <strong>1-HP healing pillar</strong> with knives/chins so she cannot heal through your Iban damage. Between specials, cast Iban Blast and maintain Prayer/charges. Her fourth special teleports you in front of her and queues a hit for almost your maximum HP. Let normal damage bring you to a controlled low HP early (the Wiki suggests about 30–40 HP initially), then <strong>after the fourth teleport, equip a fresh phoenix necklace and right-click Eat the stackable nightshade during the attack wind-up, before the hitsplat</strong>. Nightshade self-damage must carry you from <em>above</em> to <em>at or below</em> 20% of maximum HP to trigger the necklace. That activation clears the queued near-max hit even though its animation finishes, and the necklace then heals about 30% maximum HP. At 20+ current HP nightshade deals 15, so aim around <strong>20% of maximum HP plus 10–15 HP</strong>; keep enough margin to survive normal attacks and heal if you drift outside that window. Practice the timing against the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Fragment_of_Seren#Phoenix_necklaces" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki animation/strategy</a>; heal, restore Prayer and use another necklace for the next cycle. Teleport out if supplies or timing are not safe. Blood Blitz, brews or a better powered staff can simplify the fight <em>if already owned</em>, but none is a Chapter 2 dependency.</p>
        <p>After the Fragment, follow the final dialogue and <strong>finish Song of the Elves completely</strong>—do not stop at the boss kill. Claim <strong>four quest points and 40,000 XP in each of the eight required skills</strong>, plus <strong>Prifddinas</strong>, its port/crystal-city travel and access to the Gauntlet, Zalcano and elven dungeon/resources as <em>unlocks</em>, not tasks to begin here. Record rewards against the live skill tab rather than projecting exact post-quest levels.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">Chapter 2 complete · guaranteed handoff</div>
        <h3>Prifddinas is open. Stop here.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Quests/access:</strong> Regicide, Roving Elves, Mourning's End I/II and Song of the Elves complete; <strong>Prifddinas unlocked</strong>. Also retain full Fairytale II, Making History, Defender of Varrock, Dream Mentor, A Tail of Two Cats and the earlier mandatory quest chains.</li>
          <li><strong>Actual levels:</strong> at least <strong>70</strong> in all eight Song skills (Agility, Construction, Farming, Herblore, Hunter, Mining, Smithing, Woodcutting); <strong>70 Prayer, 70 Defence, 60 Ranged, 51 Slayer and 67 Sailing</strong>. Other post-quest levels vary with real XP—read the skill tab.</li>
          <li><strong>Combat/travel kit:</strong> Piety, Barrows gloves, dragon defender, Helm of Neitiznot, Proselyte, Ava's accumulator, upgraded Iban's staff, camphor-hulled skiff, Ectophial, Drakan's medallion, Blisterwood flail, Salve (e), Book of the Dead and the Weiss herb patch.</li>
          <li><strong>Intentional Chapter 3 deferrals:</strong> Path of Glouphrie plus its <strong>actual 56 Slayer</strong> catch-up; Curse of Arrav; Sailing beyond 67; Construction beyond 70; Chapter 3-specific Mining, Smithing and ship upgrades; and Mage Arena II if still desired. These are not missing Chapter 2 checkboxes.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The next project task is a <strong>full Chapter 2 → Chapter 3 retrospective dependency audit</strong> against the current Chapter 3 source. Do that before freezing either side of the boundary; do not begin Chapter 3.1 from this page.</p>
      </section>

